# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00194 Task 2.0b: the host's pingbus kit (seat disconnected) for the ccy launcher's exit,
# and the member kit's settings with the longer SessionEnd bound. Plan 00203 Task 3.10: the
# same kit (used by cc --teams and cc --bus) takes the pingbus whose SessionStart hook records
# each session's conversation, so a cc session can be restored and restarted by its own
# conversation id. Teams and homeservers are not changed. Before play-claude-yolo.yml.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml

# Plan 00194 Task 2.0b: the goodbye is no longer cut off when a session ends with Ctrl-C, and a
# session ended without it (podman stop, a closed terminal, a crash) is told "disconnected" by
# the launcher. ccy also refuses, with a clear message, a wrapper that runs a shell launcher
# through Python, instead of failing with a bare traceback.
# Plan 00203 Tasks 3.10-3.12: ccy-sessions restore resumes each session by its recorded
# conversation id, never --continue; a session with none recorded is named and not started.
# New `ccy-teams restart <team>` and the team menu's "Restart the team's desktop sessions":
# running ccy sessions restart in place at their next idle moment, stopped ones start resuming
# their conversation, running cc sessions and LXC members are left as they are and named. The
# image switches Claude Code's agent view off (/background, --bg).
# CCY 3.99.12.17, container 2.77.13, so the image IS rebuilt on the next launch. Running
# sessions are not touched.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
